Among the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/26/apple-homepod-software-27-2/">flurry</a> of <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/26/apple-releases-ios-27-2/">iOS 27.2</a> <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/26/apple-releases-macos-golden-gate-27-2/">releases</a> on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/26/apple-releases-tvos-27-2/">Monday</a>, Apple also pushed a wave of software updates for its older operating systems, including a fix for a CoreGraphics vulnerability that Apple says may have been exploited in targeted attacks. <br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2023/05/bug-security-vulnerability-issue-fix-larry.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-896108" /><br/>
The releases include iOS 26.7.2, iPadOS 26.7.2, iOS 18.7.11, iPadOS 18.7.11, macOS Tahoe 26.7.2, macOS Sequoia 15.8.2, and tvOS 26.6.1.<br/>
<br/>
<a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/149225">iOS 18.7.11 and iPadOS 18.7.11</a> bring the CoreGraphics fix to the iPhone XS, iPhone XS Max, iPhone XR, and seventh-generation iPad, all of which cannot run iOS 26. According to Apple, processing a maliciously crafted file on these devices could lead to arbitrary code execution, and the company is "aware of a report that this issue may have been exploited in an extremely sophisticated attack against specific targeted individuals on versions of iOS before iOS 27."<br/>
<br/>
For iOS 26.7.2 and iPadOS 26.7.2, Apple lists <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/123075">security fixes covering 134 vulnerabilities</a>, none of which are flagged as having been exploited in the wild. <br/>
<br/>
Apple likewise lists security fixes for <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/122868">macOS Tahoe 26.7.2</a> and <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/120283">macOS Sequoia 15.8.2</a>.<br/>
<br/>
Lastly, <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/106336">tvOS 26.6.1</a>: the only release of these updates with a user-facing change. The update adds support for the fourth-generation Siri Remote on the Apple TV HD and first-generation Apple TV 4K.<br/>
<br/>
